docs: 
#### docstext ####
text: 
The metadata schema used by Zenodo was extended with fields based on the [CodeMeta](https://codemeta.github.io/) standard, providing support for software-specific metadata.

Moreover, Zenodo supports `CITATION.cff` and `.zenodo.json` files for software releases originating from GitHub or GitLab, enhancing the integration and making the content easier to cite.

**Important:** If both files are present in your repository, **only** the `.zenodo.json` metadata will be used for the GitHub or GitLab release archiving. The `CITATION.cff` metadata will be ignored by Zenodo. See the individual pages below for more details on when to use each format.

Find more information about citing content here:

- [Referencing and citing content (GitHub)](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/archiving-a-github-repository/referencing-and-citing-content)
- About CITATION files
    - [GitHub](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-citation-files)
    - [GitLab](https://docs.gitlab.com/releases/19/gitlab-19-6-released/#citationcff-file-detection)

These are the supported methods to describe software records:
